      "content": "i hear what you're saying, but it doesn't feel that simple. when i look at them, i just see all the things they gave up for me, and now i'm just the one person who couldn't make it work. it feels like every time i try to fix things, i just cause more damage. it's like i'm a permanent parasite on their happiness. wouldn't it be more honorable to just... let them move on without the constant reminder of my failure? it feels like the only way to actually protect them is to stop being the source of their disappointment.",
